## 3 Problem Statement

We consider a known state representation q∈𝒬⊆ℝnqq\in\mathcal{Q}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n\_{q}} for a deformable object of interest (e.g., 3D positions of links for rope, or of mesh node positions for cloth) actuated by control input u∈𝒰⊆ℝnuu\in\mathcal{U}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n\_{u}} and governed by uncertain dynamics ([1a](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.14188v1#S3.E1.1 "In 1 ‣ 3 Problem Statement ‣ Robustness without Wrinkles: Parallel Simulation and Robust MPC for Certified Deformable Manipulation")), where f:𝒬×𝒰→𝒬f:\mathcal{Q}\times\mathcal{U}\rightarrow\mathcal{Q}. To account for perception latency, we model the system as being observed with uncertain time-delayed measurements y∈𝒴⊆ℝnyy\in\mathcal{Y}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n\_{y}} according to an observation map h:𝒬→𝒴h:\mathcal{Q}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y} ([1b](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2606.14188v1#S3.E1.2 "In 1 ‣ 3 Problem Statement ‣ Robustness without Wrinkles: Parallel Simulation and Robust MPC for Certified Deformable Manipulation")),

